                            automation.
                        </div>
                        <div class="work-actions">
                            <button class="btn btn-success" onclick="triggerAutomation(4)">
                                <i class="fas fa-play"></i> Trigger Implementation
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="work-item approved" style="margin-bottom: 15px;">
                        <div class="work-header">
                            <div class="work-title">Project Dashboard MVP</div>
                            <span class="status-badge status-approved">Ready for Trigger</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="work-description">
                            Dashboard design approved. Click below to trigger GitHub deployment
                        </div>
                        <div class="work-actions">
                            <button class="btn btn-success" onclick="triggerAutomation(5)">
                                <i class="fas fa-rocket"></i> Trigger Deployment
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Review Modal -->
    <div id="review-modal" class="modal">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <div class="modal-title">Review Work</div>
                <button class="close-modal" onclick="closeModal()">×</button>
            </div>
            <div id="modal-content">
                <!-- Dynamic content will be loaded here -->
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <script>
        // Sample data
        const works = {
            1: {
                title: "TheDealWizard.com Promotion Strategy",
                agent: "Marketing Boss",
                status: "review",
                progress: 100,
                description: "Complete low-cost promotion strategy for $500 Amazon gift card contest.",
                content: `## Promotion Strategy Document

### Channels Selected:
1. **Reddit Communities** - r/beermoney, r/sweepstakes
2. **Facebook Groups** - Contest & Giveaway groups
3. **Twitter Hashtags** - #giveaway #contest #amazongiftcard
4. **Partnership Outreach** - Related websites/blogs

### Budget Allocation:
- Reddit ads: $50
- Facebook boosted posts: $30
- Partnership incentives: $20
- Total: $100

### Timeline:
- Week 1: Setup & initial posts
- Week 2: Partnership outreach
- Week 3: Social media push
- Week 4: Final promotion & winner selection

### Expected Results:
- 500+ contest entries
- 50+ website signups
- 20+ social media shares
- 5+ partnership mentions`,
                automation: "Execute promotion channels across selected platforms"
            },
            2: {
                title: "Small Business Financing Email Templates",
                agent: "Content Writer",
                status: "review",
                progress: 100,
                description: "5 email templates for cold outreach to small businesses.",
                content: `## Email Campaign Package

### Template 1: Initial Outreach
**Subject:** Quick question about your business financing
**Body:** Personalized introduction + value proposition

### Template 2: Follow-up (3 days)
**Subject:** Following up on financing options
**Body:** Additional benefits + case study

### Template 3: Value-add (7 days)
**Subject:** Free financing assessment
**Body:** Offer free analysis + testimonials

### Template 4: Final attempt (14 days)
**Subject:** Last chance for special offer
**Body:** Limited-time offer + urgency

### Template 5: Breakup (21 days)
**Subject:** Closing your file
**Body:** Polite closure + future availability

### Compliance Notes:
- CAN-SPAM compliant
- GDPR considerations included
- Opt-out instructions clear
- No misleading claims`,
                automation: "Set up email sequences in campaign software"
            },
            3: {
                title: "DrugDoctors.com Home Page Design",
                agent: "Web Developer",
                status: "review",
                progress: 40,
                description: "Home page design for pharmaceutical information website.",
                content: `## Design Specifications

### Layout Structure:
1. **Hero Section** - Large banner with search
2. **Features Grid** - 4 key features with icons
3. **Latest Articles** - 3-column article previews
4. **Disclaimer Section** - Medical disclaimer
5. **Footer** - Navigation & contact

### Technical Details:
- Responsive design (mobile-first)
- CSS Grid/Flexbox layout
- Font: Open Sans / Poppins
- Color scheme: Medical blue/white
- Loading time: < 2 seconds

### Pages to Build:
1. Home page (current)
2. Drug information pages
3. Side effects database
4. Interaction checker
5. Blog/articles section

### Next Steps:
- Complete remaining pages
- Add JavaScript functionality
- Implement search feature
- SEO optimization`,
                automation: "Continue development of additional pages"
            },
            4: {
                title: "AllAboutMD.com Automation System Design",
                agent: "Operations Boss",
                status: "approved",
                progress: 100,
                description: "Automation system design for daily content generation.",
                content: `## System Architecture

### Components:
1. **Content Pipeline** - AI-assisted article generation
2. **News Aggregation** - RSS feed processing
3. **Social Automation** - Multi-platform posting
4. **Quality Control** - Editorial review system

### Technical Requirements:
- AI API integration (OpenAI/Claude)
- RSS parser implementation
- Social media APIs (FB, IG, Twitter, Pinterest)
- WordPress REST API
- Database for scheduling

### Implementation Phases:
1. MVP (4 weeks) - Basic automation
2. Enhancement (4 weeks) - Advanced features
3. Scaling (4 weeks) - Full automation
4. Optimization (ongoing) - Continuous improvement

### Cost Estimate:
- Development: $10,000-$20,000
- Monthly: $400-$1,200
- ROI: 50-200% traffic increase in 6 months`,
                automation: "Begin technical implementation phase"
            },
            5: {
                title: "Project Dashboard MVP",
                agent: "Web Developer",
                status: "approved",
                progress: 100,
                description: "Minimum viable product for project tracking dashboard.",
                content: `## Dashboard Features

### Current Version:
- Project status tracking
- Agent work display
- Progress visualization
- Basic workflow management

### Deployment Ready:
- Single HTML file
- Self-contained CSS/JS
- No external dependencies
- Mobile responsive

### GitHub Pages Deployment:
1. Create private repository
2. Upload index.html
3. Enable GitHub Pages
4. Add password protection

### Future Enhancements:
1. Real-time updates
2. Database integration
3. User authentication
4. Advanced analytics
5. API integrations`,
                automation: "Deploy to GitHub Pages with password protection"
            }
        };
        
        // Tab management
        function showTab(tabName) {
            // Hide all tabs
            document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(tab => {
                tab.style.display = 'none';
            });
            
            // Remove active class from all tabs
            document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(tab => {
                tab.classList.remove('active');
            });
            
            // Show selected tab
            document.getElementById(`${tabName}-tab`).style.display = 'block';
            
            // Add active class to clicked tab
            event.target.classList.add('active');
        }
        
        // Modal functions
        let currentWorkId = null;
        
        function reviewWork(workId) {
            currentWorkId = workId;
            const work = works[workId];
            
            document.getElementById('modal-content').innerHTML = `
                <div>
                    <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
                        <div style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 5px;">${work.title}</div>
                        <div style="color: var(--text-muted);">Submitted by: ${work.agent}</div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="work-preview">
                        ${work.content}
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="comment-section">
                        <h4 style="margin-bottom: 10px;">Add Comment/Feedback</h4>
                        <textarea class="comment-input" rows="3" placeholder="Add your comments or feedback here..."></textarea>
                        <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px;">
                            <button class="btn btn-success" onclick="approveWork(${workId})">
                                <i class="fas fa-check"></i> Approve
                            </button>
                            <button class="btn btn-warning" onclick="requestEdit(${workId})">
                                <i class="fas fa-edit"></i> Request Edit
                            </button>
                            <button class="btn btn-danger" onclick="rejectWork(${workId})">
                                <i class="fas fa-times"></i> Reject
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            `;
            
            document.getElementById('review-modal').style.display = 'flex';
        }
        
        function closeModal() {
            document.getElementById('review-modal').style.display = 'none';
            currentWorkId = null;
        }
        
        // Workflow actions
        function approveWork(workId) {
            const work = works[workId];
            
            // Update status
            work.status = 'approved';
            
            // Show success message
            alert(`✅ "${work.title}" has been approved!\n\nAutomation trigger: ${work.automation}`);
            
            // Update UI
            updateWorkItem(workId);
            
            // Close modal if open
            closeModal();
            
            // In production, this would trigger actual automation
            console.log(`Automation triggered for work ${workId}: ${work.automation}`);
        }
        
        function requestEdit(workId) {
            const work = works[workId];
            const comment = document.querySelector('.comment-input')?.value || 'No specific feedback provided';
            
            // Update status (in real system, would go back to draft)
            work.status = 'review'; // Keep in review for now
            
            // Show edit request message
            alert(`✏️ Edit requested for "${work.title}"\n\nFeedback: ${comment}\n\nWork has been sent back to ${work.agent} for revisions.`);
            
            // Update UI
            updateWorkItem(workId);
            
            // Close modal if open
            closeModal();
        }
        
        function rejectWork(workId) {
            const work = works[workId];
            const comment = document.querySelector('.comment-input')?.value || 'No specific reason provided';
            
            // Update status
            work.status = 'review'; // In real system, might have 'rejected' status
            
            // Show rejection message
            alert(`❌ "${work.title}" has been rejected.\n\nReason: ${comment}\n\nWork has been sent back to ${work.agent}.`);
            
            // Update UI
            updateWorkItem(workId);
            
            // Close modal if open
            closeModal();
        }
        
        function triggerAutomation(workId) {
            const work = works[workId];
            
            // Show automation trigger message
            alert(`⚡ Automation triggered for "${work.title}"\n\nAction: ${work.automation}\n\nAutomation process has been started.`);
            
            // Update status to show automation in progress
            work.status = 'published'; // In real system, might have 'executing' status
            
            // Update UI
            updateWorkItem(workId);
            
            // In production, this would start the actual automation
            console.log(`Starting automation for work ${workId}: ${work.automation}`);
            
            // Simulate automation completion after delay
            setTimeout(() => {
                alert(`✅ Automation completed for "${work.title}"\n\nThe automation process has finished successfully.`);
            }, 2000);
        }
        
        function updateWorkItem(workId) {
            const work = works[workId];
            const workElement = document.querySelector(`.work-item[data-id="${workId}"]`);
            
            if (workElement) {
                // Update status badge
                const badge = workElement.querySelector('.status-badge');
                badge.className = `status-badge status-${work.status}`;
                badge.textContent = work.status.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + work.status.slice(1);
                
                // Update border color
                workElement.className = `work-item ${work.status}`;
                
                // Update actions based on status
                const actions = workElement.querySelector('.work-actions');
                if (actions) {
                    if (work.status === 'approved') {
                        actions.innerHTML = `
                            <button class="btn btn-success" onclick="triggerAutomation(${workId})">
                                <i class="fas fa-play"></i> Trigger Automation
                            </button>
                            <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="reviewWork(${workId})">
                                <i class="fas fa-eye"></i> View Details
                            </button>
                        `;
                    } else if (work.status === 'published') {
                        actions.innerHTML = `
                            <button class="btn btn-success" disabled>
                                <i class="fas fa-check"></i> Automation Complete
                            </button>
                        `;
                    }
                }
            }
            
            // Refresh counts
            updateCounts();
        }
        
        function updateCounts() {
            // Count items in each status
            const counts = {
                review: 0,
                approved: 0,
                published: 0
            };
            
            Object.values(works).forEach(work => {
                if (counts[work.status] !== undefined) {
                    counts[work.status]++;
                }
            });
            
            // Update badge counts
            const reviewBadge = document.querySelector('.card-header .status-review');
            const approvedBadge = document.querySelector('.card-header .status-approved');
            
            if (reviewBadge) {
                reviewBadge.textContent = `${counts.review} items`;
            }
            
            if (approvedBadge) {
                approvedBadge.textContent = `${counts.approved} items`;
            }
        }
        
        // Initialize
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            updateCounts();
            
            // Close modal on outside click
            document.getElementById('review-modal').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
                if (e.target === document.getElementById('review-modal')) {
                    closeModal();
                }
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>